                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support>
                                    <p>Double-faced marble relief with Men on ram and solar divinity, broken on the left (from the point of view of the side which showed Men). Height 45 cm., width 44.5 cm. Known since at least 1893. For sale in New York in 1968; now returned to Münzen und Medaillen, Basel.</p>
                                    <material ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html">marble</material>
                                    <objectType ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/24.html">relief</objectType>
                                    <dimensions unit="cm">
                                        <height>45</height>
                                        <width>44,5</width>
                                        <depth></depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>
                                    <p>Relief on both faces within aedicula: one side shows foreparts of ram with crescent and four worshippers; other side shows solar divinity in quadriga. Traces of inscription on architrave.</p>
                                    <rs ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">incisa a scalpello</rs>
                                </layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
